※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4205 LANG_TYPE_OPERAND_NOT_INTEGER
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4206 LANG_TYPE_OPERAND_MISMATCH

※ A floating-point type says the value is a number, not the bits it is kept
※ in, so the operators that are questions about bits are not defined on one:
※ the bitwise operators, the shifts and the rotations.  Neither are the
※ saturating operators, whose answer is the nearest end of a range of whole
※ numbers, nor `%`, which is what is left of a division that stopped at one.

let a: f64 = 1.5f64
let b: f64 = 0.5f64

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    @[ignore(5005)]
    a & b
    @[ignore(5005)]
    a % b
    @[ignore(5005)]
    a ⊞ b
    @[ignore(5005)]
    a « 2u8
    0u6
